    "innovation": "This paper provides a region-specific quantitative assessment of biodiversity-climate interactions in the South Caucasus by integrating biodiversity structure, ecosystem function, and climate variability indicators into a single empirical, spatial, and modeling-based framework.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "NASA Earth Exchange (NEX-GDDP)",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "mean annual temperature anomaly (AT)",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Climate variability was characterized using two primary indicators: mean annual temperature anomaly (AT) and precipitation variability (AP). These variables were selected because they represent the dominant climatic stressors influencing biodiversity patterns and ecosystem functional stability in semi-arid, arid and mountainous ecosystems typical of the South Caucasus region. Climate data were obtained from the NASA Earth Exchange Global Daily Downscaled Projections (NEX-GDDP) dataset. Climate indicators were aggregated to annual values and interpolated to a spatial resolution of 0.5\u00b0 (~50 km grid scale) to ensure temporal consistency with long-term climate projection datasets covering the period 2000-2025.",
