            "paragraph": "Ecosystem functional indicators were represented using three key variables: Primary productivity (NPP) - used as an indicator of ecosystem energy flow and biological production capacity. Soil organic carbon stock (SOC) - used as a proxy for long-term ecosystem carbon storage and soil functional stability. Moisture index (MI) - used to represent hydrological balance and vegetation water availability under climate variability. NPP estimates were derived from satellite-based productivity models and harmonized with climate datasets. SOC data were obtained from the FAO Global Soil Database and aggregated to match climate spatial units. The moisture index was calculated based on precipitation-evapotranspiration balance metrics derived from climate observations.",
